course: dictionary
lesson: 1385
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The words around it, its context, tell you which meaning is right. «Brightly coloured liquid capsules for washing machines have been mistaken for sweets by small children.» Washing machines and liquid tell you this capsule is a small container of washing liquid, not a sweet and not a medicine.
explain: «After 2011 Russian Soyuz capsules, and later SpaceX capsules, kept taking crews to the space station.» Taking crews to a space station is a clue that a capsule is a part of a spacecraft where astronauts sit. Always ask: which meaning fits the words around it? Then put that meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Some words are shared by very different things. Capsule can mean a medicine you swallow, a spacecraft part, a box for the future, or a seed case in a plant. Safety matters too: never take capsules or tablets unless a trusted adult gives them to you.
fact: A capsule is a small tube-shaped container, such as a medicine you swallow.
fact: A space capsule is a small part of a spacecraft where astronauts sit, and it can come back to Earth.
fact: A time capsule is a box of things kept for people in the future to open.
fact: In plants, a capsule is a seed case that splits open.
fact: Laundry capsules and coffee pods are dangerous if swallowed, so keep them away from small children.
exercise: «Brightly coloured liquid capsules for washing machines have been mistaken for sweets.» What is a capsule in this sentence? | *A small container of washing liquid | A sweet to eat | A seed case that splits open | A part of a spaceship
exercise: «After 2011 Russian Soyuz capsules kept taking crews to the space station.» What is a capsule here? | A tablet you swallow | A box buried for people in the future | A seed case in a plant | *A part of a spacecraft where astronauts sit
exercise: In class, pupils make a time capsule to open later. What is a time capsule? | A seed case that splits open | *A box of things kept for people in the future to open | A coffee pod | A medicine you swallow
test: «A capsule in a plant splits open to release its seeds.» What is a capsule in this sentence? | A laundry pod | A part of a spacecraft | *A seed case that splits open | A small container of medicine
test: Safety rule: what should you do with a capsule or tablet unless a trusted adult gives it to you? | *Leave it alone and tell a trusted adult | Share it with your friends | Take one to feel better | Swallow it quickly to check it
exam: «The astronauts came safely back to Earth in their capsule.» What does capsule mean here? | A box of things kept for the future | *A part of a spacecraft where astronauts sit | A seed case in a plant | A small tube of medicine
